 "drivingQuestion": "Why are final waters obligatory?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "eruvin.17b.6",
   "daf": "17b",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "אָמַר רַב חִיָּיא בַּר אָשֵׁי: מִפְּנֵי מָה אָמְרוּ מַיִם אַחֲרוֹנִים חוֹבָה? מִפְּנֵי שֶׁמֶּלַח סְדוֹמִית יֵשׁ, שֶׁמְּסַמֵּא אֶת הָעֵינַיִם.",
   "en": "«Rav Ḥiyya bar Ashi said: For what» reason «did» the Sages «say that the final waters are an obligation?» It is «due to» the fact «that there is the presence of Sodomite salt, which blinds the eyes» even in a small amount. Since Sodomite salt could remain on one’s hands, one must wash them after eating. This obligation is binding even in a camp because soldiers are also obligated to maintain their health."
  },
  {
   "id": "eruvin.17b.7",
   "daf": "17b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "אָמַר אַבָּיֵי: וּמִשְׁתַּכְחָא כְּקוּרְטָא בְּכוֹרָא. אֲמַר לֵיהּ רַב אַחָא בְּרֵיהּ דְּרָבָא לְרַב אָשֵׁי: כָּיֵיל מִילְחָא, מַאי? אֲמַר לֵיהּ: [הָא] לָא מִיבַּעְיָא.",
   "en": "«Abaye said: And» this type of dangerous salt «is present» in the proportion of a single «grain [korta] in an» entire «kor» of innocuous salt. «Rav Aḥa, son of Rava, said to Rav Ashi:» If «one measured salt» and came into contact with Sodomite salt not during mealtime, «what» is the halakha? Is there an obligation to wash his hands afterward? «He said to him: It was unnecessary» to say «this,» as he is certainly obligated to do so."
  }
 ],
